# deml-ui — Cursor rules (design system SoT LOCKED)

This repo is the DEML design system — **single source of truth** for the
**new-from-the-start (NFTS) / heritage** look consumed by deml and Django static
chrome. **Seven-color palette only.** Do not drift to Viking or atelier-cream.

## Locked palette (exact)

`#0066B2` `#3D3D3D` `#BDBDBD` `#121212` `#FFFFFF` `#3C7A4A` `#C41E3A`

Dark/light role swaps only; mixes only among these hexes. No cream
(`#E4DDD0` / `#F4F1EA`), void (`#2A2622`), or electric (`#2176ff`).

## Do

- Change visuals in `components/<name>/` and `styles/tokens.css` / `styles/base.css`.
- Keep an 8px grid (`--grid` / `--space-*`), dual `data-theme`, **equal outer
  spacing on all four sides**, equal tile gaps (`--tile-gap` / `--module-pad`),
  identical row heights (`--tile-row-unit`), and locked chart aspect
  (`--chart-aspect: 2.4` — never squash/stretch).
- Use tokens only for chrome — `--palette-*`, `--color-*`, `--space-*`,
  `--tile-*`, `--chart-*`, `--font-*`, `--tracking-*`, `--hit-target`.
- Type hierarchy: large primary headings bold condensed tight tracking
  (`--font-display` / `--tracking-display`); secondary/intro generous
  letter-spacing (`--tracking-eyebrow` / `--tracking-intro`); readable body.
- Chart series colors from the seven-color palette only; plots inside
  equal-height chart-cards with aspect-locked containers.
- Run `npm run sync` after adding/removing component folders; `npm run build`
  before release.
- Prefer WCAG 2.0 AA patterns already used in base + headless primitives
  (focus-visible, contrast, hit targets, reduced motion).

## Do not

- Reintroduce Viking-UI naming, void-black / electric `#2176ff` suite chrome, or
  `--viking-*` tokens.
- Reintroduce atelier-cream / limestone hexes or any eighth chrome color.
- Hand-edit generated wrappers under `src/angular/markup/` or `generated/` —
  regenerate via sync.
- Break the chart aspect contract or invent one-off / asymmetric spacing outside
  the token scale.
- Ship arbitrary hex in component CSS for chrome outside the seven locked colors.

Consumer guidance for the Angular app lives in deml `THEME.md` / `AGENTS.md` /
`.cursorrules`. deml must not invent app-level DS chrome CSS.

**Locked:** deml-ui owns the NFTS / heritage look; Viking and cream atelier are
fully retired.
